{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    vector<pair<long long, long long>> candidates;\n    long double target = static_cast<long double>(x) / y;\n    \n    if (y <= 1) {\n        cout << x << '/' << y;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    for (long long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        long long num_floor = static_cast<long long>(floor(target * d));\n        long long num_ceil = static_cast<long long>(ceil(target * d));\n        candidates.push_back({num_floor, d});\n        if (num_floor != num_ceil) {\n            candidates.push_back({num_ceil, d});\n        }\n    }\n    \n    pair<long long, long long> best = {0, 1};\n    long double min_diff = 1e30;\n    \n    for (const auto& cand : candidates) {\n        long long num = cand.first;\n        long long den = cand.second;\n        if (den == 0) continue;\n        long double diff = abs(target - static_cast<long double>(num) / den);\n        if (diff < min_diff) {\n            min_diff = diff;\n            best = cand;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << best.first << '/' << best.second;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] input = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        long x = Long.parseLong(input[0]);\n        long y = Long.parseLong(input[1]);\n        long n = Long.parseLong(input[2]);\n        \n        List<long[]> candidates = new ArrayList<>();\n        double target = (double) x / y;\n        \n        if (y <= 1) {\n            System.out.println(x + \"/\" + y);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        for (long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n            long num_floor = (long) Math.floor(target * d);\n            long num_ceil = (long) Math.ceil(target * d);\n            candidates.add(new long[]{num_floor, d});\n            if (num_floor != num_ceil) {\n                candidates.add(new long[]{num_ceil, d});\n            }\n        }\n        \n        long[] best = new long[]{0, 1};\n        double min_diff = 1e30;\n        \n        for (long[] cand : candidates) {\n            long num = cand[0];\n            long den = cand[1];\n            if (den == 0) continue;\n            double diff = Math.abs(target - (double) num / den);\n            if (diff < min_diff) {\n                min_diff = diff;\n                best = cand;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(best[0] + \"/\" + best[1]);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013672371278516948, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00025614796322770417, -1.811964830267243e-05, -0.03674953430891037, -0.5525752902030945, -0.000